# Migration-header commands that predate lint-migration-commands.sh.
#
# Format: `<migration-path>#<despaced-command>  <reason>`, one per line.
# The key is printed by the gate on failure, so an entry is copied rather
# than hand-derived. The reason field is REQUIRED.
#
# SHRINK-ONLY. Adding a line needs a `Baseline-Growth:` commit trailer
# naming this file (scripts/ci/lint-baseline-growth.sh), and a line whose
# command has gone away — or has since gained a test that names its
# migration and holds a verbatim slice of it — is STALE and fails the
# gate until it is deleted.
#
# 151 migrations predate the rule; 10 of them carry header commands, and
# migrations/0156_prices_1m_retention.{up,down}.sql is the one already
# covered (internal/storage/timescale/retention_policy_test.go pins its
# arm, its disarm, its `force => true` recovery and its DO-NOT-RUN form).
# The way to shrink this file is to write that test for the next one.
#
# CURRENT STATE: 46 entries across 18 migration files.

